  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 20-layer alternating MgF2/HfO2 stack on fused silica substrate under air incidence. Layer sequence: MgF2, HfO2, MgF2, HfO2, MgF2, HfO2, MgF2, HfO2, MgF2, HfO2, MgF2, HfO2, MgF2, HfO2, MgF2, HfO2, MgF2, HfO2, MgF2, HfO2 (20 finite layers). Initialize thicknesses on a linear chirp from 140 nm (layer 1) to 50 nm (layer 20). Apply per-layer thickness bounds of ±5 nm around the chirp trajectory. Optimize all 20 thicknesses to maximize mean transmittance in 255-280 nm while minimizing mean transmittance in 300-700 nm and 700-1100 nm bands. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer. Evaluate coherent TMM response across 255-1100 nm spectrum. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 255-280 nm, 300-700 nm, 700-1100 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 255–280 nm; low transmittance in 300–700 nm; low transmittance in 700–1100 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 300–700 nm; transmittance in 700–1100 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30; no metal layers; conventional depositable inorganic dielectric materials only.",
